            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 667)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Cancel a web share.</b> A Cancel button sits beside the progress bar in the Shared Review panel. Canceling a first share removes what was uploaded, as if it had never started; canceling a re-share leaves the link that is already live exactly as it was.</li>
<li><b>&#8220;Link may keep a copy on the viewer&#8217;s device&#8221; is live.</b> It used to be fixed when the share started. Now you can change it at any point: turn it off and open pages stop saving and delete the copy they hold; turn it on and they start saving, with no reload. A viewer who is offline picks it up the next time they open the link.</li>
<li><b>Notes in order of scope.</b> The sidebar now has two fields instead of one with a globe switch: <b>Session note (whole review)</b> at the top, and the note for the frame you are on at the bottom, beside the transport. The web page is laid out the same way.</li>
<li><b>On the web:</b> a second repeat button &#8212; this clip or all clips &#8212; beside the once / loop / ping-pong button, as in the app; and clips now play all the way to their last frame, so short clips loop properly.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
